<!-- The nyeb adversary-complaint Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs; docs/EVAL-LOOP.md,
     "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}: Times New Roman, was EB Garamond) at 12 pt (size 24
     half points; no FRBP or E.D.N.Y. LBR sets a face or size, both filed exemplars use 12 pt Times); Body Text in exact
     24 pt line boxes (typst pitch-body, double spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single
     lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single). Replaced or added here, as the typst template sets them: the three
     heading levels at the type size on the body pitch, 12 pt above (typst heading-above), kept with the text after
     them (1 and 2 centred bold, as typed; 3 bold italic); "Body Text Keep" (the prayer's lead-in, kept with its
     items); "Allegation" (Fed. R. Civ. P. 10(b): the number at the indent, a tab to 1 in, the text hanging there;
     typst labelled) and "Allegation Keep" (the last paragraph, kept with the signature). Letter page (E.D.N.Y. LBR
     9004-1(a)(ii)), 1 in margins, the page number centred in a single-pitch line whose box ends 0.5 in above the page
     edge (typst footer-distance). The caption and the signature block carry their own spacing
     (docx/nyeb-adversary-complaint.lua). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
